]], ["", [], []], ["", [], []], ["", [], []], ["", [], []], ["SPEM cell vs antral basal gland mucous cell", [], "The marker sets are the SAME (AQP5, CD44/CD44v9, MUC6, TFF2). PMID 40803502: 'These markers are expressed in normal deep antral glands'. The distinction is REGIONAL/contextual, not transcriptional: AQP5+/MUC6+ gland-base mucous cells are normal in the ANTRUM and metaplastic (SPEM) in the CORPUS, where they replace parietal and chief cells."], ["SPEM cell vs mucous neck cell", [], "PMID 40803502 states explicitly that GSII, MUC6 and TFF2 'are also expressed in the mucous neck cells of the corpus'. Only AQP5 and CD44v9 separate SPEM from normal neck cells, and both are also positive in normal deep antral glands."], ["incomplete vs complete intestinal metaplasia", [], "PMID 40803502: incomplete GIM is AQP5/CD44v9-positive at the gland base and expresses TROP2 (TACSTD2) and basolateral CEACAM5 but is 'negative for CD10 and DEFA5'; complete GIM has NO SPEM markers and expresses CDH17, TFF3 and CD10 (MME). PMID 40691053: incomplete IM cells co-express gastric CLDN18 and intestinal FABP2."], ["tuft cell vs enteroendocrine cell", [], "Both are rare solitary epithelial cells concentrated in the isthmus. Tuft cells are POU2F3/TRPM5/AVIL(+DCLK1) and CHGA-negative; gastric EECs are CHGA/CHGB+ with a single dominant hormone (GAST/SST/GHRL/HDC/TPH1)."]], "oq": [], "ca": [], "sa": [{"name": "osteoclastogenic RANKL program", "markers": ["TNFSF11", "ETS1"], "pmids": ["40136507", "38554844"], "applies_to": ["mesenchymal cell"], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": []}, {"name": "type 2/22 cytokine program", "markers": ["IL13", "IL22", "IL4", "IL5", "GATA3"], "pmids": ["26242300"], "applies_to": ["T cell"], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": []}, {"name": "proliferating", "markers": ["MKI67", "TOP2A", "CCNB1", "CENPF"], "pmids": ["12058064"], "applies_to": [], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": ["tissue-resident macrophage", "basal keratinocyte", "fibrobl